{
  "id": "30513_tsuijuku",
  "headword": "追熟",
  "reading": "ついじゅく",
  "romaji": "tsuijuku",
  "part_of_speech": "noun",
  "gloss": "post-harvest ripening; after-ripening",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "post-harvest ripening; after-ripening",
      "explanation": "The practice of letting fruit finish ripening after it has been picked, by leaving it at room temperature for a few days. Used of kiwis, avocados, melons, bananas and similar fruit that are shipped unripe."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "30513_tsuijuku_ex1",
      "japanese": "アボカドを{追熟|ついじゅく}させる。",
      "english": "I let the avocado ripen.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "30513_tsuijuku_ex2",
      "japanese": "キウイは{常温|じょうおん}で{追熟|ついじゅく}します。",
      "english": "Kiwis ripen at room temperature.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "30513_tsuijuku_ex3",
      "japanese": "{硬|かた}いうちに{買|か}って、{食|た}べ{頃|ごろ}まで{追熟|ついじゅく}させるとよい。",
      "english": "It is best to buy them while they are still firm and let them ripen until they are ready to eat.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "A produce and cooking term. It appears mostly on packaging, in recipes, and at greengrocers rather than in everyday conversation.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {追熟|ついじゅく}させる: to let something ripen\n- {追熟|ついじゅく}が{進|すす}む: for ripening to advance\n- {常温|じょうおん}で{追熟|ついじゅく}する: to ripen at room temperature\n- {追熟|ついじゅく}{期間|きかん}: ripening period\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {熟|じゅく}す: to ripen — the general verb, on or off the tree\n- {完熟|かんじゅく}: fully ripe — the finished state rather than the process",
